00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:07.859
Let's go next to why don't we go to Victor
from Indiana.

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:08.980
You're on the air.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.429
Hi, David.

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:16.770
So I was wondering, how married are you to
the idea of social democracy or having a social

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:20.500
welfare programs under the framework of capitalism?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.500
I'm I'm married.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.720
I'm I'm married to it, but I have a prenup
and an annulment clause so I could get out

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.630
if it got ugly.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.630
I see.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.630
Got it.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.050
No, I mean, sorry I cut you off.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:37.370
So you're saying it sounded like you were
saying how married am I to social democracy

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.530
rather than socialism?

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:45.100
Sort of, I guess my main question was, do
you think socialism or even something like

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:51.110
communism is feasible for human society, like
maybe like a couple hundred like a thousand

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.220
years down the line?

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.150
Or do you just think that, like, capitalism
is pretty much the best we've got right now?

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.320
It's not worth talking about.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:04.119
OK, so here's where I'm different from many
other commentators on this issue, lots of

00:01:04.119 --> 00:01:05.119
commentators.

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:10.430
You would go to them and you would ask that
question and some people would say communism

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.990
is an inevitability.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.030
It's just a matter of when.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.700
And there are others on the right.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.170
And by the way, you've got a horrible, horrible
hiss coming through.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.640
And if we could deal with that, it would it
would be a really great thing.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.820
Yeah, then you've got people on the right,
including Trump, I mean, Trump said it during

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:33.060
his state of the unions that states of the
Union addresses whatever Trump said, we will

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.799
never be a socialist country.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:39.620
I am not going to pretend to tell you that
something definitely could or couldn't happen

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.020
a thousand years down the line.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.510
If you asked anybody in the United States,
there was no United States a thousand years

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.510
ago.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:49.850
If you asked people a thousand years ago in
twenty twenty one, would there be something

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.220
like the United States?

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.690
Would we have the technology we have?

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.689
Would we have the culture we have?

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:56.979
Nobody would have predicted this a thousand
years ago.

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.530
And so I have no idea.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:05.950
I don't I think that right now everything
has led me to my current beliefs, which, as

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.050
you state, fall under the umbrella of social
democracy.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.869
That's where I am right now.

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:14.599
Is it possible that things will happen in
the next two hundred or thousand years where

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:20.680
in a thousand years the planet, planet Earth
is a socialist planet, is a communist planet,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.109
or there are many communist countries that
that are flourishing?

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:25.769
Yeah, it's how could I say no?

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:26.769
How could it?

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:32.900
So I just think that we are so bad at predicting
the future that it's certainly possible.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.669
And if that happens, I, I don't know what
the path to it would be.

00:02:37.669 --> 00:02:40.799
That's a fantastic answer.

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:41.799
Thank you so much, David.

00:02:41.799 --> 00:02:42.799
All right, my pleasure.

00:02:42.799 --> 00:02:43.799
Great having you on.

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:46.559
And that's that's an ugly history there that
was happening.

00:02:46.559 --> 00:02:49.009
I'm glad we were able to get it, at least
briefly dealt with.

